# Regenerable NF-FASTPATH outputs — the projection lives in the S3 lake
# (nfl/fantasy/derived/season_projections); the human-readable deliverable is the
# ablation_results report. These are rebuilt by run_season_projection.py.
*.parquet
*.csv
*_summary.json

# Per-season backfill summaries. The *_summary.json rule above does not match the backfill
# naming (..._summary_<year>.json), which is how these escaped it.
*_summary_*.json

# NF-W7e per-fold marginal-bank cache (regenerable; ~70 MB/fold)
nf_w7e_bank_cache/

# NF-INJ2 working directory: the per-arm 2026 boards plus the SERVED-artifact baseline copies the
# reproduction pin is measured against. All regenerable by
# `run_nf_inj2_rate_permutation.py` — and the served copies are snapshots of artifacts the board
# build already owns, so committing them would fork a second vintage of the same board.
nf_inj2_baseline/

# NF-C6-PH2 — the weekly serving BUILD OUTPUT. Regenerated by every run and published to the
# api-cache; the record that belongs in git is `ablation_results/nf_c6_ph2_promotion_review.*`,
# not the payload. Same treatment as `draft_board_json/`, which is likewise untracked.
weekly_serving/

# NF-INJ4b-SHIP — the ship battery's capture of the SERVED board. The MANIFEST beside it IS tracked
# (it is the vintage record the NF-INJ2c preconditions read, and it is 22 KB); the 1.3 MB board
# payload is not, for the same reason `nf_inj2_baseline/` is not — it is a snapshot of an artifact
# the board build already owns, and committing it forks a second vintage of the same board.
# ⚠️ Re-stage it with the command in `ablation_results/nf_inj4b_ship_battery.md`. Note that this
# re-stages the CURRENT board, which after the ADP day rolls is a DIFFERENT one (NF-INJ2c: a vendor
# snapshot is not recoverable once its day passes) — the manifest is what says which board the
# battery's numbers describe.
nf_inj4b_ship_baseline/*
!nf_inj4b_ship_baseline/manifest.json
